## Lore

Light Machines are the Warlords'' human-sized cyborgs. A full conversion keeps
the proportions of a person, so it can wear ordinary clothes and body armor,
ride a horse or a hovercycle and sit in a normal car, and many keep a human
face. That makes them the War Camps'' augmented soldiers, agents and spies, as
well as their rank and file.

In Russia bionics carry no stigma. Cyborgs are seen as patriots who gave up
their bodies to defend people, and most Light Machines show their machine
parts openly, like a badge. The acceptance keeps them steady: they tend to
hold on to their families, their friends and their sense of who they were.

## GM Notes

The body is the `warlord-light-machine-cyborg` vessel row: 170 M.D.C. main
body, head 80, arms 60, legs 85, with the two concealed Vibro-Blades and the
ion wrist blaster. Bionic P.S. is 28-30 and P.P. 20-24; set them when the
character is built.

Partial conversions count as Light Machines too. The 55% package (one bionic
arm, both legs, a reinforced frame of 15 M.D.C.) costs a Warlord about
300,000 credits; the 70-80% package (both arms, both legs, a 65 M.D.C. torso)
about 500,000. Both wear light cyborg armor of 140 M.D.C. or ordinary body
armor.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: all the ammunition and equipment
for the body''s weapon systems, an energy rifle of choice, four grenades of
choice, and a long coat, cap or hat, scarf, gloves and boots worn for show or
disguise. Maintenance and repairs are free in a Warlord''s service. Money is
6D6x10 credits plus 3D6x10 in tradeable goods; pay is 900-1300 credits a
month by rank and record.

A jet pack, a hover vehicle and more weapons may be issued by assignment. A
Light Machine with no Warlord behind him starts with one less weapon, one
less head feature and no Gromeko identification computer, and buys his own
upgrades.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'warlord-light-machine');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'warlord-light-machine';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-warlord-light-machine-class.sql');
